      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "### Problem\n\nIn [Fennel 1.6](https://fennel-lang.org/changelog#160--2025-10-13) they added `fnlm` as an official file extension for macro files. Before that, it was all `fnl`. `fnlm` currently doesn't set the filetype to `fennel` when you open it.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nTreat `fnlm` the same `fnl`, since they're literally identical syntactically.\n\n### Manual Fix\n\nJust add the following in your `init.fnl` or `init.lua`\n```clj\n(vim.filetype.add {:extension {:fnlm :fennel}})\n```\n```lua\nvim.filetype.add { extension = { fnlm = \"fennel\" } }\n```",
